# Keeps the Docker build context small. nginx/Dockerfile only needs
# Frontend/Dashboard/, Frontend/Landingpage/, nginx/, and this Dockerfile
# itself (it runs its own `npm install` inside each build stage, so local
# node_modules aren't needed) — everything below is safe to exclude.
#
# NOTE: bare patterns in .dockerignore only match at the build-context
# root (unlike .gitignore's implicit recursion) — every pattern here that
# also needs to match in subdirectories (e.g. Backend/.env,
# Backend/logs/*.log) uses an explicit **/ prefix. Verified empirically.

.git
**/node_modules
**/*.log
**/__pycache__
**/.env
**/.env.*
